{"id": "EUVD-2026-86942", "enisaUuid": "e94cf5bb-fa45-379a-9f0b-06726e59114b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: btintel: validate version TLV value lengths\n\nbtintel_parse_version_tlv() verifies that a complete TLV is present in\nthe response, but it does not ensure that the value is long enough for\nthe specific TLV type. A short value can therefore cause an\nout-of-bounds read through get_unaligned_le16(), get_unaligned_le32(),\nor memcpy().\n\nReject values shorter than the minimum required by each known TLV type.\nAlso reject responses that do not contain the Command Complete Status\nfield.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:35:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:14:03", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e9cf7f175c00d36b060828f4eac8d2e246ee079b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/83499ac3ca62e43ed40f7574b13ed398a6891511", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/76948d207d0978a613ce06a05cba07284a5578a7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5ec43df2830b73e004147303bf7914ca884d6770", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a086c0892969bf8a0151b0f12bd14a68827c88b2"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98111", "GHSA-r6wm-2pr2-7xgp"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "388b1dc4-2b3c-3a70-885a-ff100a0a04e7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "57375beef71af9f245e88357fa71d9600650cb7d <76948d207d0978a613ce06a05cba07284a5578a7"}, {"id": "532f2c42-8f2f-369c-b5fb-e1922cc60355", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10"}, {"id": "6d20285e-6067-3100-9750-b53d090a1008", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "57375beef71af9f245e88357fa71d9600650cb7d <5ec43df2830b73e004147303bf7914ca884d6770"}, {"id": "760be761-a057-3787-ad52-2a508be66425", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "8bdf8f35-53b0-3d85-a741-